      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e cached state that differentiate the first run from the subsequent runs\n\nIf you are testing the state preservation between 2 subsequent runs of a non-protected VM, then shouldn\u0027t we be actually persisting the instance-id to ensure non-protected VM follow the same code path as protected VM?\n\nOTOH, if you\u0027re non preserving states between 2 runs of test vms, how about allocating random 64 bytes\u0027? I think it would be good to avoid default 0s for instanceId.\n\nAlso, will you add a check in virtmgr to ensure that instanceId is non-0s?",
