        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T11:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Each allocation of `instance_id` creates an entry in VS\u0027 database, once the instance-id is obsolete, it should be removed from the db.\n\nCan you trigger `removeVmInstance`[1] when this instance is no more needed? [This might be tricky though, because that will be the decision of a caller]. If this is only used for testing, maybe we can call `removeVmInstance` after `VmInstance::create` ?\n\n\nWhat is the use case of non-protected service_vm? Does it not require persistence (as in hinted by instance.img being a temp file)?\n\n\n[1] https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/virtualizationservice/aidl/android/system/virtualizationservice_internal/IVirtualizationServiceInternal.aidl;l\u003d110?q\u003dremoveVmInstance\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 331,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 331,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "de057a6c6b2149dfa886cf1313f7752566bf18c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
