      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T15:28:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e removeVmInstance is not available in VirtualizationService and it looks like it\u0027s not called anywhere yet.\n\nits available in `IVirtualizationServiceInternal`.\n\n\u003e I can work on this part after you finishing the removal part of instance id\n\nI\u0027ll probably work on removeVmInstance first \u0026 instance.img removal last. But yeah, SG. Would you add a TODO(b/xx) so that we rememeber where all to trigger `removeVmInstance` from?\n\n\n\u003e renaming the method to something more specific such as removeVmInstanceId()?\n\nThe purpose of that method is really to remove all global state related to the instance. In case of service_vm, this maybe just instance_id, but in case of Microdroid based VM, it will include deleting Secretkeeper based secrets, so I think the name of the method is just fine.\n\n\u003e and it doesn\u0027t actually remove the vm_instance\n\n`removeVmInstance` should be triggered when the instance is no longer needed \u0026 should be obsolete. fn `nonprotected_vm_instance` seems to be using temporary file for instance.img too indicating the instance really becomes obsolete immediately after the file goes out of scope i.e, when the method ends.",
