      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T11:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about we move this method to libvmclient, so that other users of the library such as /vm/src/run.rs can also use it directly? Also if we can get `instance_starter.rs` to use this, we will be able to cut on fragmentation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "de057a6c6b2149dfa886cf1313f7752566bf18c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65f2e956_5c1d6093",
        "filename": "service_vm/manager/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T13:38:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "About this, why not just take the instanceId file descriptor in the config like instance image? Then you can internalize all the `if exist { read } else { allocate }` logic all somewhere instead of letting each caller repeats similar code?\n\nIf it\u0027s handled internally, you can also ensure that `allocateInstanceId` is always called for the instance ID creation. With the current config format, people are not always aware that `#allocateInstanceId` is required for the id creation.",
      "parentUuid": "454c9948_e2ddd25c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "de057a6c6b2149dfa886cf1313f7752566bf18c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98e85a48_7cdc5ec6",
        "filename": "service_vm/manager/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T15:28:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e why not just take the instanceId file descriptor in the config like instance image\n\nI think passing around 64 bytes of data instead of fd is a more robust api. Converting the instanceId into parcels early ensure it is the right size etc.\n\n\nFrom what I gather, the reason instance.img  is passed around as fd is because it is formatted by VS \u0026 backs a virtio-blk device which is written on my VM. instance-id is a read-only data in the VM\u0027s device tree as far as VM is concerned.\n\n\u003e With the current config format, people are not always aware that #allocateInstanceId is required for the id creation\n\n\u003e you can also ensure that allocateInstanceId is always called for the instance ID creation.\n\nEven then there is nothing preventing a client to write 64 bytes into instanceId file \u0026 use that VM run. We should check for default allocation of VM instance is prevented by checking instanceId as suggested in other comment.",
      "parentUuid": "65f2e956_5c1d6093",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "de057a6c6b2149dfa886cf1313f7752566bf18c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
