      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T11:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggestion: `get_or_create` like methods are failure prone \u0026 hide the diagnostic information at times. Do you have any other signal to indicate that a new VM Id should be allocated (perhaps new VM created or something?). Otherwise if presence or absence or the file is the only indicator of a new VM being created, can we add a `log::warn!()` on else arm of the logic, specifying the new instance_id is being created. This is because it essentially resets the VM, the key blobs can no longer be decrypted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "de057a6c6b2149dfa886cf1313f7752566bf18c9",
